{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit `theta ~ uniform(0, 1);` prior before the likelihood. This is density-neutral for `theta`, which is already constrained to `[0, 1]`, and satisfies SafeStan's requirement that each parameter have exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before use. `K` and `N` remain context data. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> K;
  array[K] int<lower=0> N;
  array[K] int<lower=0> y;
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[K] theta;
}
model {
  theta ~ uniform(0, 1);
  y ~ binomial(N, theta);
}
generated quantities {
  array[K] int<lower=0, upper=1> is_best;
  {
    real best_prob = max(theta);
    for (k in 1 : K) {
      is_best[k] = theta[k] >= best_prob;
    }
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"K":5,"N":[2,4,2,3,3],"y":[2,3,2,3,3]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
